    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i already checked the filter and its totally clean. the manual says e15 means water is in the base tray underneath the unit. how do i get to that tray and dry it out?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Locating the base tray requires tilting the dishwasher forward and keeping your hand over the top opening to prevent water from spraying down onto your hand. Once there, scoop out the standing water from the reservoir bucket and hose down the three drainage holes at the base of the tray to clear any remaining debris or partial obstructions. After ensuring the tray and pump area are dry, close the dishwasher and run a short cycle with a salt level setting that matches the humidity in your region to reset the system and re-establish proper drainage. If the error returns immediately after the cycle completes, the water discharge valve may need replacement.",
